<title>USA: Heilig-Meyers files $400 mln shelf.</title>
<headline>Heilig-Meyers files $400 mln shelf.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Heilig-Meyers Co on Tuesday registered with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission for a shelf offering of up to $400 million in common stock and warrants to purchase common shares.</p>
<p>In addition, the company's subsidiary, MacSaver Financial Services Inc, would be able to issue debt securities under the shelf registration.</p>
<p>The company, a home-furnishing retailer, will use proceeds from the sale for general corporate purposes, which may include repaying oustanding debt, capital expenditures and possible acquisitions.</p>
<p>No underwriters were named in the filing.</p>
</text>
